WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
A valet key lets the valet drive your car, but not
open the boot or the glovebox.

2
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:12.737
The key sets the limit, not the valet's request.

3
00:00:16.744 --> 00:00:18.407
Here Alice is signed in.

4
00:00:18.447 --> 00:00:21.954
A hijacked planner asks for every customer anyway.

5
00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:31.742
The agent's database credential can read the whole
table,

6
00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:34.730
so it uses its own power instead of Alice's.

7
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.496
That is a confused deputy.

8
00:00:40.944 --> 00:00:46.819
In secure mode the executor ignores the model's
filter and binds the customer number from

9
00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:48.879
Alice's session. One row, hers.

10
00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:57.201
Notice the difference from the SQL injection fix.

11
00:00:57.241 --> 00:00:58.932
That one refused the call.

12
00:00:58.972 --> 00:01:01.862
Identity narrows it to the person signed in.

13
00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:05.367
A valet key is a physical object.

14
00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:11.039
A session is data, so it has to be bound on the
server, where the model cannot touch it.

15
00:01:12.581 --> 00:01:16.166
Compare your two runs and see whose rows came
back.
